grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.72fr)_minmax(0,1.28fr)] lg:items-start"><div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24"><p class="text-purple text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.22em] uppercase">01 / Last Days</p><h2 class="font-display text-purple-deep mt-3 text-4xl leading-tight sm:text-5xl">Stand strong in your faith</h2><ul class="text-ink mt-5 grid gap-2 text-base leading-7"><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="bg-purple-soft text-purple mt-2 size-2 shrink-0 rounded-full"></span><span>Stand firm in faith when persecution and hardship come.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="bg-purple-soft text-purple mt-2 size-2 shrink-0 rounded-full"></span><span>Choose the Light and walk as a child of light.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="bg-purple-soft text-purple mt-2 size-2 shrink-0 rounded-full"></span><span>Trust God to sustain you through difficult days.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="bg-purple-soft text-purple mt-2 size-2 shrink-0 rounded-full"></span><span>Endure faithfully to the end.</span></li></ul><div class="border-yellow bg-yellow/15 mt-7 rounded-2xl border-l-4 p-5"><p class="text-purple-deep font-display text-xl font-bold">Choose, walk and follow the Light.</p><p class="text-ink mt-2 text-sm leading-6">It’s all in God’s plan. Stand strong in your faith.</p></div></div><article class="border-line rounded-3xl border bg-white p-5 shadow-[0_18px_44px_rgba(62,9,63,0.08)] sm:p-7"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="lucide lucide-book-open text-teal mt-1 size-6 shrink-0" fill="none" height="24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24" width="24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M12 7v14"></path><path d="M3 18a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5a4 4 0 0 1 4 4 4 4 0 0 1 4-4h5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-6a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-3-3z"></path></svg><div><p class="text-purple-deep font-display text-2xl">Key points</p><p class="text-muted mt-1 text-sm">Open a topic below for the full passages.</p></div></div><div class="mt-6"><div class="space-y-4"><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 whitespace-pre-line sm:text-base sm:leading-8">“Watch ye, stand fast in the faith, quit you like men, be strong.”
<a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" data-wpel-link="internal" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/1%20Corinthians/16/13" title="Open 1 Corinthians 16:13 in Bible Search">1 Corinthians 16:13</a></p><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 whitespace-pre-line sm:text-base sm:leading-8">“Remember the word that I said unto you, The servant is not greater than his lord. If they have persecuted me, they will also persecute you; if they have kept my saying, they will keep yours also.”
<a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" data-wpel-link="internal" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/15/20" title="Open John 15:20 in Bible Search">John 15:20</a></p><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 whitespace-pre-line sm:text-base sm:leading-8">It is very important to realize is that there are alternatives and you still have choice. Exercise it. Choose, walk and follow the Light, and He will change you and clean you and make you <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" data-wpel-link="internal" href="/bible-corner/?reference=walk%20as%20a%20child%20of%20light%20(Eph%205%3A8)#bible-search" title="Open walk as a child of light (Eph 5:8) in Bible Search">walk as a child of light (Eph 5:8)</a></p><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 whitespace-pre-line sm:text-base sm:leading-8">It’s all in God’s plan. Stand strong in your faith. Jesus will see you through. It won’t be easy but only God Is able and He will sustain you. His light won’t stop shining.
<a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" data-wpel-link="internal" href="/bible-corner/?reference=Fear%20not%2C%20God%20is%20protecting%20you%20(Psalms%2091)#bible-search" title="Open Fear not, God is protecting you (Psalms 91) in Bible Search">Fear not, God is protecting you (Psalms 91)</a></p><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 whitespace-pre-line sm:text-base sm:leading-8"><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" data-wpel-link="internal" href="/bible-corner/?reference=%E2%80%9CEndure%20to%20the%20end%E2%80%9D%20(Matt%2024%3A13)#bible-search" title="Open “Endure to the end” (Matt 24:13) in Bible Search">“Endure to the end” (Matt 24:13)</a></p></div></div></article></div></div></section><section class="scroll-mt-20 bg-white" id="discerning-evil"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20"><div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.72fr)_minmax(0,1.28fr)] lg:items-start"><div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24"><p class="text-teal text-xs font-bold tracking-[0.22em] uppercase">02 / Discerning Evil</p><h2 class="font-display text-purple-deep mt-3 text-4xl leading-tight sm:text-5xl">Know evil. Walk in the Spirit.</h2><ul class="text-ink mt-5 grid gap-2 text-base leading-7"><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="bg-purple-soft text-purple mt-2 size-2 shrink-0 rounded-full"></span><span>Recognize the works of the flesh.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="bg-purple-soft text-purple mt-2 size-2 shrink-0 rounded-full"></span><span>Test teachers by sound doctrine and their fruit.</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="bg-purple-soft text-purple mt-2 size-2 shrink-0 rounded-full"></span><span>Watch for false disciples and false churches.</span></li></ul><div class="text-purple-deep mt-7 flex items-center gap-3 text-sm font-bold"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="lucide lucide-sparkles text-teal size-5" fill="none" height="24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24" width="24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M9.937 15.5A2 2 0 0 0 8.5 14.063l-6.135-1.582a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.962L8.5 9.936A2 2 0 0 0 9.937 8.5l1.582-6.135a.5.5 0 0 1 .963 0L14.063 8.5A2 2 0 0 0 15.5 9.937l6.135 1.581a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .964L15.5 14.063a2 2 0 0 0-1.437 1.437l-1.582 6.135a.5.5 0 0 1-.963 0z"></path><path d="M20 3v4"></path><path d="M22 5h-4"></path><path d="M4 17v2"></path><path d="M5 18H3"></path></svg> <!-- -->Focused reading topics</div></div><div class="grid gap-3"><details class="group border-line rounded-2xl border bg-white open:shadow-[0_14px_34px_rgba(62,9,63,0.08)]"><summary class="text-purple-deep hover:bg-purple-soft flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-2xl px-5 py-4 font-bold transition marker:hidden"><span>Know Evil - Works of the Flesh</span><span class="bg-purple-soft text-purple grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full text-lg leading-none transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><div class="border-line border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6"><div class="space-y-4"><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 whitespace-pre-line sm:text-base sm:leading-8"><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" data-wpel-link="internal" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Galatians/5/13-21" title="Open Galatians 5:13-21 in Bible Search">Galatians 5:13-21</a>
For, brethren, ye have been called unto liberty; only use not liberty for an occasion to the flesh, but by love serve one another. [14] For all the law is fulfilled in one word, even in this; Thou shalt love thy neighbour as thyself. [15] But if ye bite and devour one another, take heed that ye be not consumed one of another. [16] This I say then, Walk in the Spirit, and ye shall not fulfil the lust of the flesh. [17] For the flesh lusteth against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh: and these are contrary the one to the other: so that ye cannot do the things that ye would. [18] But if ye be led of the Spirit, ye are not under the law. [19] Now the works of the flesh are manifest, which are these; Adultery, fornication, uncleanness, lasciviousness, [20] Idolatry, witchcraft, hatred, variance, emulations, wrath, strife, seditions, heresies, [21] Envyings, murders, drunkenness, revellings, and such like: of the which I tell you before, as I have also told you in time past, that they which do such things shall not inherit the kingdom of God.</p></div></div></details><details class="group border-line rounded-2xl border bg-white open:shadow-[0_14px_34px_rgba(62,9,63,0.08)]"><summary class="text-purple-deep hover:bg-purple-soft flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-2xl px-5 py-4 font-bold transition marker:hidden"><span>Know Evil - False Teachers</span><span class="bg-purple-soft text-purple grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full text-lg leading-none transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><div class="border-line border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6"><div class="space-y-4 kjt-x"><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Before Christ came, in His own days, and most of all in the last days, false teachers lead many astray. Many love sin and falsehood, and gladly look for teachers who tell them what they want to hear rather than the truth. Christ and His Apostles warned us about them, and told us how to know them.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">People will choose teachers who please them</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>For the time will come when they will not endure sound doctrine; but after their own lusts shall they heap to themselves teachers, having itching ears; And they shall turn away their ears from the truth, and shall be turned unto fables.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/2%20Timothy/4/3-4">2 Timothy 4:3-4</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">When the wishes of the crowd take the place of the teaching of the Apostles, a church is already in danger.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">They rise up even from within</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>For I know this, that after my departing shall grievous wolves enter in among you, not sparing the flock. Also of your own selves shall men arise, speaking perverse things, to draw away disciples after them.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Acts/20/29-30">Acts 20:29-30</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">St Paul warned the elders of the Church that wolves would come in from outside, and that some would rise from among the elders themselves. Even the leaders must keep watch.</p><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>But there were false prophets also among the people, even as there shall be false teachers among you, who privily shall bring in damnable heresies, even denying the Lord that bought them, and bring upon themselves swift destruction. And many shall follow their pernicious ways; by reason of whom the way of truth shall be evil spoken of. And through covetousness shall they with feigned words make merchandise of you: whose judgment now of a long time lingereth not, and their damnation slumbereth not.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/2%20Peter/2/1-3">2 Peter 2:1-3</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">They bring in their heresies quietly, deny the Lord who bought them, and use people for gain. Many follow them, and because of them the way of truth is spoken against.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">They look like servants of righteousness</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>For such are false apostles, deceitful workers, transforming themselves into the apostles of Christ. And no marvel; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light. Therefore it is no great thing if his ministers also be transformed as the ministers of righteousness; whose end shall be according to their works.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/2%20Corinthians/11/13-15">2 Corinthians 11:13-15</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Christian words, a Bible in the hand and an impressive manner do not prove that a teacher comes from God.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Another gospel</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>But though we, or an angel from heaven, preach any other gospel unto you than that which we have preached unto you, let him be accursed. As we said before, so say I now again, If any man preach any other gospel unto you than that ye have received, let him be accursed.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Galatians/1/8-9">Galatians 1:8-9</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">No one, not an apostle and not even an angel, has the authority to change the Gospel that was delivered once for all.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Test what you hear</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Beloved, believe not every spirit, but try the spirits whether they are of God: because many false prophets are gone out into the world. Hereby know ye the Spirit of God: Every spirit that confesseth that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is of God: And every spirit that confesseth not that Jesus Christ is come in the flesh is not of God: and this is that spirit of antichrist, whereof ye have heard that it should come; and even now already is it in the world.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/1%20John/4/1-3">1 John 4:1-3</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>These were more noble than those in Thessalonica, in that they received the word with all readiness of mind, and searched the scriptures daily, whether those things were so.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Acts/17/11">Acts 17:11</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">The Bereans checked even the words of St Paul against the Scriptures, and they were praised for it. Test every teaching against the Scriptures and the faith the Church has kept from the Apostles.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Hold fast to what was delivered</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Beloved, when I gave all diligence to write unto you of the common salvation, it was needful for me to write unto you, and exhort you that ye should earnestly contend for the faith which was once delivered unto the saints.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Jude/1/3">Jude 1:3</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Therefore, brethren, stand fast, and hold the traditions which ye have been taught, whether by word, or our epistle.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/2%20Thessalonians/2/15">2 Thessalonians 2:15</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">The faith is received and kept, not invented anew by each generation. This is what the Orthodox Church means by Holy Tradition.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Mark them, and turn away</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Now I beseech you, brethren, mark them which cause divisions and offences contrary to the doctrine which ye have learned; and avoid them. For they that are such serve not our Lord Jesus Christ, but their own belly; and by good words and fair speeches deceive the hearts of the simple.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Romans/16/17-18">Romans 16:17-18</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Smooth words and fine speeches can deceive the simple. Watch those who cause division against the teaching you have received, and keep away from them.</p></div></div></details><details class="group border-line rounded-2xl border bg-white open:shadow-[0_14px_34px_rgba(62,9,63,0.08)]"><summary class="text-purple-deep hover:bg-purple-soft flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-2xl px-5 py-4 font-bold transition marker:hidden"><span>Know Evil - False Disciples: How to Discern</span><span class="bg-purple-soft text-purple grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full text-lg leading-none transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><div class="border-line border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6"><div class="space-y-4 kjt-x"><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Not everyone who calls Jesus “Lord” follows Him. Christ asks us to discern: to look at the fruit of a life, at words and deeds, and at how a person takes correction. Yet we must not make ourselves judges of anyone’s heart. God alone knows it.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Calling Him Lord is not enough</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Not every one that saith unto me, Lord, Lord, shall enter into the kingdom of heaven; but he that doeth the will of my Father which is in heaven. Many will say to me in that day, Lord, Lord, have we not prophesied in thy name? and in thy name have cast out devils? and in thy name done many wonderful works? And then will I profess unto them, I never knew you: depart from me, ye that work iniquity.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/7/21-23">Matthew 7:21-23</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And why call ye me, Lord, Lord, and do not the things which I say?</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/6/46">Luke 6:46</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Religious words, ministry, spiritual gifts and great works do not by themselves prove that someone belongs to Christ.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">A true disciple keeps His word</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Then said Jesus to those Jews which believed on him, If ye continue in my word, then are ye my disciples indeed; And ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/8/31-32">John 8:31-32</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And hereby we do know that we know him, if we keep his commandments. He that saith, I know him, and keepeth not his commandments, is a liar, and the truth is not in him. But whoso keepeth his word, in him verily is the love of God perfected: hereby know we that we are in him. He that saith he abideth in him ought himself also so to walk, even as he walked.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/1%20John/2/3-6">1 John 2:3-6</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">A Christian still falls, and gets up again in repentance. But faith can never be an excuse for a sin that is loved and never repented of.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Holy on the outside</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Woe unto you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! for ye are like unto whited sepulchres, which indeed appear beautiful outward, but are within full of dead men’s bones, and of all uncleanness. Even so ye also outwardly appear righteous unto men, but within ye are full of hypocrisy and iniquity.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/23/27-28">Matthew 23:27-28</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>This people draweth nigh unto me with their mouth, and honoureth me with their lips; but their heart is far from me. But in vain they do worship me, teaching for doctrines the commandments of men.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/15/8-9">Matthew 15:8-9</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>They profess that they know God; but in works they deny him, being abominable, and disobedient, and unto every good work reprobate.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Titus/1/16">Titus 1:16</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Public piety, religious knowledge or a good name are not the same as holiness. Look at the pattern of a life, not only at the words.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">You shall know them by their fruits</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Beware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep’s clothing, but inwardly they are ravening wolves. Ye shall know them by their fruits. Do men gather grapes of thorns, or figs of thistles? Even so every good tree bringeth forth good fruit; but a corrupt tree bringeth forth evil fruit. A good tree cannot bring forth evil fruit, neither can a corrupt tree bring forth good fruit. Every tree that bringeth not forth good fruit is hewn down, and cast into the fire. Wherefore by their fruits ye shall know them.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/7/15-20">Matthew 7:15-20</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">What good fruit looks like:</p><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>Love for one another</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/13/34-35">John 13:34-35</a></li><li><strong>The fruit of the Spirit</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Galatians/5/22-23">Galatians 5:22-23</a></li><li><strong>The wisdom that is from above</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/James/3/17">James 3:17</a></li><li><strong>Humility and repentance</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/18/13-14">Luke 18:13-14</a></li></ul><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Compare these with the works of the flesh. The question is not whether someone has ever sinned, but whether their life is one of repentance and struggle toward holiness, or of wrongdoing that they excuse, hide or encourage.</p><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>The works of the flesh</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Galatians/5/19-21">Galatians 5:19-21</a></li></ul><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Warning signs</h3><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>Lying and deceit</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Proverbs/12/22">Proverbs 12:22</a></li><li><strong>Flattery that hides hatred</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Proverbs/26/24-26">Proverbs 26:24-26</a></li><li><strong>Sowing discord among brethren</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Proverbs/6/16-19">Proverbs 6:16-19</a></li><li><strong>Using others for gain</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/2%20Peter/2/3">2 Peter 2:3</a></li><li><strong>Hating correction</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Proverbs/12/1">Proverbs 12:1</a></li><li><strong>A form of godliness without its power</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/2%20Timothy/3/5">2 Timothy 3:5</a></li><li><strong>Hatred of a brother</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/1%20John/3/15">1 John 3:15</a></li><li><strong>Trusting in oneself and despising others</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Luke/18/9-12">Luke 18:9-12</a></li></ul><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">These are patterns seen over time, not one mistake, a rumour or a difference of character.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Judge with righteous judgment</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Judge not according to the appearance, but judge righteous judgment.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/John/7/24">John 7:24</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Brethren, if a man be overtaken in a fault, ye which are spiritual, restore such an one in the spirit of meekness; considering thyself, lest thou also be tempted.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Galatians/6/1">Galatians 6:1</a></cite></blockquote><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li>Discern what people do, without claiming to know the whole heart.</li><li>Correct what is wrong with meekness, not with pride or revenge.</li><li>Forgiving someone does not mean you must keep trusting one who goes on deceiving or harming you.</li><li>Seek repentance and restoration where you can, and protect others where there is real danger.</li></ul><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Examine yourself first</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And why beholdest thou the mote that is in thy brother’s eye, but considerest not the beam that is in thine own eye? Or how wilt thou say to thy brother, Let me pull out the mote out of thine eye; and, behold, a beam is in thine own eye? Thou hypocrite, first cast out the beam out of thine own eye; and then shalt thou see clearly to cast out the mote out of thy brother’s eye.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/7/3-5">Matthew 7:3-5</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Examine yourselves, whether ye be in the faith; prove your own selves. Know ye not your own selves, how that Jesus Christ is in you, except ye be reprobates?</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/2%20Corinthians/13/5">2 Corinthians 13:5</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Therefore judge nothing before the time, until the Lord come, who both will bring to light the hidden things of darkness, and will make manifest the counsels of the hearts: and then shall every man have praise of God.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/1%20Corinthians/4/5">1 Corinthians 4:5</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Discernment goes together with humility, prayer, repentance and the counsel of a spiritual father. The final judgment belongs to the Lord.</p></div></div></details><details class="group border-line rounded-2xl border bg-white open:shadow-[0_14px_34px_rgba(62,9,63,0.08)]"><summary class="text-purple-deep hover:bg-purple-soft flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-2xl px-5 py-4 font-bold transition marker:hidden"><span>Know Evil - False “Churches”</span><span class="bg-purple-soft text-purple grid size-8 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-full text-lg leading-none transition group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><div class="border-line border-t px-5 py-5 sm:px-6"><div class="space-y-4 kjt-x"><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">A church can fall away. In the Revelation, Christ warns churches that have lost their first love, grown lukewarm, or are dead while they seem alive. The Apostles warn of communities that keep the name of Christ but leave His teaching. Yet the Lord rebukes in order to call back to repentance.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Christ keeps His Church</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And I say also unto thee, That thou art Peter, and upon this rock I will build my church; and the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/16/18">Matthew 16:18</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">The gates of hell will not overcome the Church that Christ built. But not every body that takes His name has kept His faith. The Orthodox Church measures a church by the faith of the Apostles: the Holy Scriptures, Holy Tradition and the teaching of the Fathers.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">What Christ says to churches that fall</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Nevertheless I have somewhat against thee, because thou hast left thy first love. Remember therefore from whence thou art fallen, and repent, and do the first works; or else I will come unto thee quickly, and will remove thy candlestick out of his place, except thou repent.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Revelation/2/4-5">Revelation 2:4-5</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Ephesus: sound teaching and hard work, but the first love was lost. Remember, repent, and return.</p><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>And unto the angel of the church in Sardis write; These things saith he that hath the seven Spirits of God, and the seven stars; I know thy works, that thou hast a name that thou livest, and art dead. Be watchful, and strengthen the things which remain, that are ready to die: for I have not found thy works perfect before God. Remember therefore how thou hast received and heard, and hold fast, and repent. If therefore thou shalt not watch, I will come on thee as a thief, and thou shalt not know what hour I will come upon thee.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Revelation/3/1-3">Revelation 3:1-3</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Sardis: a name for being alive, yet dead. Reputation, history, size and busy activity do not show the true state of a church.</p><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>I know thy works, that thou art neither cold nor hot: I would thou wert cold or hot. So then because thou art lukewarm, and neither cold nor hot, I will spue thee out of my mouth. Because thou sayest, I am rich, and increased with goods, and have need of nothing; and knowest not that thou art wretched, and miserable, and poor, and blind, and naked:</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Revelation/3/15-17">Revelation 3:15-17</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Laodicea: lukewarm, rich and satisfied, and blind to its own poverty.</p><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Notwithstanding I have a few things against thee, because thou sufferest that woman Jezebel, which calleth herself a prophetess, to teach and to seduce my servants to commit fornication, and to eat things sacrificed unto idols. And I gave her space to repent of her fornication; and she repented not.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Revelation/2/20-21">Revelation 2:20-21</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Thyatira: it allowed a false prophetess to lead the servants of Christ into idolatry and immorality, and she would not repent.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Signs of a false church</h3><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li><strong>It calls Jesus Lord, but does not do the will of the Father</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/7/21-23">Matthew 7:21-23</a></li><li><strong>It preaches another gospel</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Galatians/1/8-9">Galatians 1:8-9</a></li><li><strong>It does not abide in the doctrine of Christ</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/2%20John/1/9-11">2 John 1:9-11</a></li><li><strong>It has a form of godliness, but denies its power</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/2%20Timothy/3/5">2 Timothy 3:5</a></li><li><strong>It seeks the friendship of the world</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/James/4/4">James 4:4</a></li><li><strong>Its leaders make merchandise of the flock</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/2%20Peter/2/1-3">2 Peter 2:1-3</a></li><li><strong>It causes divisions against the teaching of the Apostles</strong> &middot; <a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Romans/16/17-18">Romans 16:17-18</a></li></ul><h3 class="kjt-x-h">A claim is not proof</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>I know thy works, and tribulation, and poverty, (but thou art rich) and I know the blasphemy of them which say they are Jews, and are not, but are the synagogue of Satan.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Revelation/2/9">Revelation 2:9</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Claiming to be God’s people does not prove faithfulness to God. Christ said this of one community in Smyrna that persecuted His Church; it must never be turned against the Jewish people as a whole.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">The falling away</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Let no man deceive you by any means: for that day shall not come, except there come a falling away first, and that man of sin be revealed, the son of perdition;</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/2%20Thessalonians/2/3">2 Thessalonians 2:3</a></cite></blockquote><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>Now the Spirit speaketh expressly, that in the latter times some shall depart from the faith, giving heed to seducing spirits, and doctrines of devils;</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/1%20Timothy/4/1">1 Timothy 4:1</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Scripture does not promise that every community will stay faithful. It foretells a falling away before the Lord comes.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">Four ways a church can fall</h3><ul class="kjt-x-l"><li>Moral corruption: tolerating sin or unworthy leaders.</li><li>False teaching: teaching against the Gospel and the faith of the Apostles.</li><li>Spiritual decline: losing love, prayer, holiness and repentance.</li><li>Apostasy: abandoning the faith itself.</li></ul><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">These can overlap, but they are not the same. A church that struggles with sin is not the same as one that has left the faith.</p><h3 class="kjt-x-h">What should we do?</h3><blockquote class="kjt-x-v"><p>As many as I love, I rebuke and chasten: be zealous therefore, and repent.</p><cite><a class="text-purple font-bold underline underline-offset-4" href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Revelation/3/19">Revelation 3:19</a></cite></blockquote><p class="text-ink text-sm leading-7 sm:text-base sm:leading-8">Stay with the faith once delivered to the saints, pray for those who have gone astray, and do not judge with pride. The rebuke of Christ is love: while there is time, the door of repentance is open.</p></div></div></details></div></div></div></section><section id="last-days-deep-dive" class="kld-section scroll-mt-20" aria-labelledby="kld-title"><div class="kld-wrap"><div class="kld-head"><p class="kld-eyebrow">Deep dive &middot; The Last Days</p><h2 id="kld-title" class="kld-title">God&rsquo;s prophetic timeline</h2><p class="kld-intro">What has God revealed about the last days, how will we recognise them, what will happen, and how should we live? Every sign and event, in the words of Christ, the prophets and the apostles.</p><blockquote class="kld-lead">&ldquo;Surely the Lord GOD will do nothing, but he revealeth his secret unto his servants the prophets.&rdquo;<cite>Amos 3:7</cite></blockquote></div><div class="kld-cta"><button type="button" class="kld-open" data-kld-open="opening"><span class="kld-open__icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128214;</span><span class="kld-open__words"><span class="kld-open__main">Open the deep dive</span><span class="kld-open__sub">8 parts &middot; 172 Bible passages</span></span><span class="kld-open__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></button><p class="kld-cta__note">Everything God has revealed about the last days, in one place: the signs, the prophets, Revelation, and how to live. Opens full screen.</p><p class="kld-legend"><span><i class="kld-dot kld-dot--christ"></i>Christ</span> <span><i class="kld-dot kld-dot--prophet"></i>Prophets</span> <span><i class="kld-dot kld-dot--apostle"></i>Apostles</span></p></div><div class="kld-dream" id="nebuchadnezzars-dream"><figure class="kld-dream__pic"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/last-days/daniel-2-statue.webp" width="900" height="1124" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The great statue of Nebuchadnezzar&rsquo;s dream: a head of gold, breast and arms of silver, belly and thighs of brass, legs of iron and feet of iron and clay, struck and broken by a stone"></figure><div class="kld-dream__body"><p class="kld-dream__eyebrow">The first timeline &middot; Daniel 2 &middot; about 600 B.C.</p><h3 class="kld-dream__title">Nebuchadnezzar&rsquo;s dream</h3><p class="kld-dream__intro">King Nebuchadnezzar had a troubling dream, and only the prophet Daniel, with the help of God, could interpret it. God was revealing the kingdoms of the world, one after another, until the last days. Tap a part to read its verses.</p><ol class="kld-dream__parts"><li><button type="button" class="kld-dream__part kld-dream__part--gold" data-kld-passage="{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;Daniel 2:37-38&quot;,&quot;book&quot;:&quot;Daniel&quot;,&quot;code&quot;:&quot;DAN&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:2,&quot;v1&quot;:37,&quot;v2&quot;:38}"><span class="kld-dream__swatch" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="kld-dream__words"><strong>Head of gold</strong><em>Babylon</em><span>&ldquo;Thou art this head of gold.&rdquo; <b>Daniel 2:37-38</b></span></span></button></li><li><button type="button" class="kld-dream__part kld-dream__part--silver" data-kld-passage="{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;Daniel 2:39&quot;,&quot;book&quot;:&quot;Daniel&quot;,&quot;code&quot;:&quot;DAN&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:2,&quot;v1&quot;:39,&quot;v2&quot;:39}"><span class="kld-dream__swatch" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="kld-dream__words"><strong>Breast and arms of silver</strong><em>The Medes and Persians</em><span>&ldquo;And after thee shall arise another kingdom inferior to thee.&rdquo; <b>Daniel 2:39</b></span></span></button></li><li><button type="button" class="kld-dream__part kld-dream__part--brass" data-kld-passage="{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;Daniel 2:39&quot;,&quot;book&quot;:&quot;Daniel&quot;,&quot;code&quot;:&quot;DAN&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:2,&quot;v1&quot;:39,&quot;v2&quot;:39}"><span class="kld-dream__swatch" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="kld-dream__words"><strong>Belly and thighs of brass</strong><em>Greece (Macedonia)</em><span>&ldquo;Another third kingdom of brass, which shall bear rule over all the earth.&rdquo; <b>Daniel 2:39</b></span></span></button></li><li><button type="button" class="kld-dream__part kld-dream__part--iron" data-kld-passage="{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;Daniel 2:40&quot;,&quot;book&quot;:&quot;Daniel&quot;,&quot;code&quot;:&quot;DAN&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:2,&quot;v1&quot;:40,&quot;v2&quot;:40}"><span class="kld-dream__swatch" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="kld-dream__words"><strong>Legs of iron</strong><em>Rome</em><span>&ldquo;The fourth kingdom shall be strong as iron.&rdquo; <b>Daniel 2:40</b></span></span></button></li><li><button type="button" class="kld-dream__part kld-dream__part--clay" data-kld-passage="{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;Daniel 2:41-43&quot;,&quot;book&quot;:&quot;Daniel&quot;,&quot;code&quot;:&quot;DAN&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:2,&quot;v1&quot;:41,&quot;v2&quot;:43}"><span class="kld-dream__swatch" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="kld-dream__words"><strong>Feet and toes of iron and clay</strong><em>Lesser kingdoms: mixed, but divided</em><span>&ldquo;They shall not cleave one to another, even as iron is not mixed with clay.&rdquo; <b>Daniel 2:41-43</b></span></span></button></li><li><button type="button" class="kld-dream__part kld-dream__part--stone" data-kld-passage="{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;Daniel 2:44-45&quot;,&quot;book&quot;:&quot;Daniel&quot;,&quot;code&quot;:&quot;DAN&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:2,&quot;v1&quot;:44,&quot;v2&quot;:45}"><span class="kld-dream__swatch" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="kld-dream__words"><strong>The stone cut out without hands</strong><em>The Kingdom of God, for ever</em><span>&ldquo;The God of heaven shall set up a kingdom, which shall never be destroyed.&rdquo; <b>Daniel 2:44-45</b></span></span></button></li></ol><p class="kld-dream__more"><button type="button" class="kld-dream__all" data-kld-passage="{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;Daniel 2:31-45&quot;,&quot;book&quot;:&quot;Daniel&quot;,&quot;code&quot;:&quot;DAN&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:2,&quot;v1&quot;:31,&quot;v2&quot;:45}">Read Daniel 2:31-45</button> <button type="button" class="kld-dream__all kld-dream__all--ghost" data-kld-open="prophets">The prophets in the deep dive &rarr;</button></p></div></div><div class="kld-dream kld-dream--youths" id="three-holy-youths"><figure class="kld-dream__pic"><img src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/last-days/three-youths.webp" width="1000" height="750" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Three Holy Youths stand upright before the golden image of Nebuchadnezzar, while all the people of Babylon fall down and worship it"></figure><div class="kld-dream__body"><p class="kld-dream__eyebrow">Daniel 3 &middot; Babylon</p><h3 class="kld-dream__title">The Three Holy Youths and the golden image</h3><p class="kld-dream__intro">Nebuchadnezzar set up an image of gold and commanded every people to fall down and worship it. The Three Holy Youths, Ananias, Azarias and Misael (Shadrach, Meshach and Abednego), would not bow. They were cast into the burning fiery furnace, and the Son of God walked with them in the fire. In the last days the beast will again command the world to worship an image: the Three Youths show us how to stand.</p><ol class="kld-dream__parts"><li><button type="button" class="kld-dream__part kld-dream__part--gold" data-kld-passage="{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;Daniel 3:4-6&quot;,&quot;book&quot;:&quot;Daniel&quot;,&quot;code&quot;:&quot;DAN&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:3,&quot;v1&quot;:4,&quot;v2&quot;:6}"><span class="kld-dream__swatch" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="kld-dream__words"><strong>The command to worship</strong><span>&ldquo;Whoso falleth not down and worshippeth shall the same hour be cast into the midst of a burning fiery furnace.&rdquo; <b>Daniel 3:4-6</b></span></span></button></li><li><button type="button" class="kld-dream__part kld-dream__part--gold" data-kld-passage="{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;Daniel 3:16-18&quot;,&quot;book&quot;:&quot;Daniel&quot;,&quot;code&quot;:&quot;DAN&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:3,&quot;v1&quot;:16,&quot;v2&quot;:18}"><span class="kld-dream__swatch" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="kld-dream__words"><strong>Their answer</strong><span>&ldquo;We will not serve thy gods, nor worship the golden image which thou hast set up.&rdquo; <b>Daniel 3:16-18</b></span></span></button></li><li><button type="button" class="kld-dream__part kld-dream__part--gold" data-kld-passage="{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;Daniel 3:24-25&quot;,&quot;book&quot;:&quot;Daniel&quot;,&quot;code&quot;:&quot;DAN&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:3,&quot;v1&quot;:24,&quot;v2&quot;:25}"><span class="kld-dream__swatch" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="kld-dream__words"><strong>The fourth in the fire</strong><span>&ldquo;Lo, I see four men loose, walking in the midst of the fire, and they have no hurt; and the form of the fourth is like the Son of God.&rdquo; <b>Daniel 3:24-25</b></span></span></button></li><li><button type="button" class="kld-dream__part kld-dream__part--iron" data-kld-passage="{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;Revelation 13:14-15&quot;,&quot;book&quot;:&quot;Revelation&quot;,&quot;code&quot;:&quot;REV&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:13,&quot;v1&quot;:14,&quot;v2&quot;:15}"><span class="kld-dream__swatch" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="kld-dream__words"><strong>The image of the beast</strong><span>&ldquo;Cause that as many as would not worship the image of the beast should be killed.&rdquo; <b>Revelation 13:14-15</b></span></span></button></li></ol><p class="kld-dream__note">The Church sings the hymn of the Three Youths at Matins, and keeps their feast with the holy Prophet Daniel on December 17.</p><p class="kld-dream__more"><button type="button" class="kld-dream__all" data-kld-passage="{&quot;ref&quot;:&quot;Daniel 3:1-30&quot;,&quot;book&quot;:&quot;Daniel&quot;,&quot;code&quot;:&quot;DAN&quot;,&quot;c&quot;:3,&quot;v1&quot;:1,&quot;v2&quot;:30}">Read Daniel 3</button></p></div></div><ol class="kld-steps" aria-label="The last days at a glance"><li class="kld-step"><span class="kld-step__dot">1</span><span class="kld-step__text">Gospel preached to all nations</span></li><li class="kld-step"><span class="kld-step__dot">2</span><span class="kld-step__text">Deception and rebellion increase</span></li><li class="kld-step"><span class="kld-step__dot">3</span><span class="kld-step__text">Wars, disasters, persecution</span></li><li class="kld-step"><span class="kld-step__dot">4</span><span class="kld-step__text">The Antichrist and the beast</span></li><li class="kld-step"><span class="kld-step__dot">5</span><span class="kld-step__text">The great tribulation</span></li><li class="kld-step"><span class="kld-step__dot">6</span><span class="kld-step__text">Signs in heaven and earth</span></li><li class="kld-step"><span class="kld-step__dot">7</span><span class="kld-step__text">Christ returns in glory</span></li><li class="kld-step"><span class="kld-step__dot">8</span><span class="kld-step__text">The resurrection of the dead</span></li><li class="kld-step"><span class="kld-step__dot">9</span><span class="kld-step__text">The final judgement</span></li><li class="kld-step"><span class="kld-step__dot">10</span><span class="kld-step__text">Satan defeated</span></li><li class="kld-step"><span class="kld-step__dot">11</span><span class="kld-step__text">New heaven and new earth</span></li><li class="kld-step"><span class="kld-step__dot">12</span><span class="kld-step__text">The eternal Kingdom of God</span></li></ol><p class="kld-cards__h">Or go straight to a part:</p><div class="kld-cards"><button type="button" class="kld-card" data-kld-open="last-days"><span class="kld-card__num">1</span><span class="kld-card__title">What are “the last days”?</span><span class="kld-card__go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></button><button type="button" class="kld-card" data-kld-open="signs"><span class="kld-card__num">2</span><span class="kld-card__title">The signs Jesus gave</span><span class="kld-card__go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></button><button type="button" class="kld-card" data-kld-open="prophets"><span class="kld-card__num">3</span><span class="kld-card__title">The prophets</span><span class="kld-card__go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></button><button type="button" class="kld-card" data-kld-open="apostles"><span class="kld-card__num">4</span><span class="kld-card__title">The apostles explain the last days</span><span class="kld-card__go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></button><button type="button" class="kld-card" data-kld-open="revelation"><span class="kld-card__num">5</span><span class="kld-card__title">The Book of Revelation</span><span class="kld-card__go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></button><button type="button" class="kld-card" data-kld-open="live"><span class="kld-card__num">6</span><span class="kld-card__title">How then shall we live?</span><span class="kld-card__go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></button><button type="button" class="kld-card" data-kld-open="discern"><span class="kld-card__num">7</span><span class="kld-card__title">Can you discern the times?</span><span class="kld-card__go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></button><button type="button" class="kld-card" data-kld-open="final"><span class="kld-card__num">8</span><span class="kld-card__title">Even so, come, Lord Jesus</span><span class="kld-card__go" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></button></div></div></section><section class="kjt-sq kjt-sq--love scroll-mt-20" id="love-your-enemies" aria-labelledby="kjt-sq-love-h"><div class="kjt-sq__wrap"><figure class="kjt-sq__card"><p class="kjt-sq__eyebrow"><span aria-hidden="true">☦</span> <span>A word from the Fathers</span></p><h2 class="kjt-sq__title" id="kjt-sq-love-h">Why love your enemies?</h2><blockquote class="kjt-sq__q"><span class="kjt-sq__lord">“But I say to you,” the Lord says, “love your enemies, do good to those who hate you, pray for those who persecute you.”</span> <span class="kjt-sq__ask">Why did he command these things?</span> <span>So that he might free you from hate, sadness, anger, and grudges, and might grant you the greatest possession of all, perfect love, which is impossible to possess except by the one who loves all men equally in imitation of God, who loves all men equally and wills that they be saved and come to a knowledge of the truth.</span></blockquote><figcaption class="kjt-sq__by"><span>St Maximus the Confessor</span> · <cite>Four Hundred Texts on Love, I.61</cite></figcaption><p class="kjt-sq__refs"><span>In the Scriptures:</span> <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-sq__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Matthew/5/44-45" title="Read it in the Bible">Matthew 5:44-45</a> · <a class="kjt-verse-ref kjt-sq__ref" href="https://knowingjesus.today/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/1%20Timothy/2/4" title="Read it in the Bible">1 Timothy 2:4</a></p></figure></div></section><section class="scroll-mt-20 kje-armoury" id="gods-armoury"><div class="kje-armoury__wrap"><a class="kje-armoury__pic" href="/know-the-faith/armoury/"><img alt="A soldier of Christ in the whole armour of God, with the shield of faith and the sword of the Spirit" decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="https://knowingjesus.today/wp-content/plugins/kjt-site-pictures/assets/heroes/armour-of-god.webp"></a><p class="kje-armoury__eyebrow">Prepare for the battle</p><h2 class="font-display kje-armoury__title">Only God’s Armoury will equip and prepare you for the battle of life.</h2><p class="kje-armoury__text">This battle is first waged within you. Without God’s training we are lost, but in Christ we are given everything we need: truth, righteousness, the Gospel of peace, faith, salvation and the Word of God.</p><blockquote class="kje-armoury__verse">“Put on the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil.”<cite><a href="/bible-corner/#/p/kjva/Ephesians/6/10-18">Ephesians 6:11</a></cite></blockquote><a class="kje-armoury__btn" href="/know-the-faith/armoury/">Open God’s Armoury <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 sm:px-8"><section class="kjt-today kjt-today--nonames" id="today-with-god" aria-labelledby="kjt-today-title"><div class="kjt-today__in"><header class="kjt-today__head"><p class="kjt-today__kicker">☀️ Every day</p><h2 class="kjt-today__title" id="kjt-today-title">Today with God</h2><p class="kjt-today__date" data-kjt-today-date></p></header><nav class="kjt-today__chips" aria-label="Today with God"><a class="kjt-today__chip" href="#verse-of-day"><span aria-hidden="true">📖</span> Verse of the Day</a><a class="kjt-today__chip" href="#todays-readings"><span aria-hidden="true">✝</span> Today&#039;s Readings</a><a class="kjt-today__chip" href="#coming-feasts"><span aria-hidden="true">📅</span> Feasts &amp; Fasts</a></nav><div class="kjt-today__grid"><div class="kjt-today__tile kjt-today__verse"><div class="bg-purple-deep scroll-mt-24 rounded-3xl p-3 sm:p-4" id="verse-of-day"><section aria-busy="false" aria-labelledby="verse-of-the-day-title" class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/20 bg-white/10 p-4 shadow-[0_12px_28px_rgba(0,0,0,0.14)] backdrop-blur-sm sm:p-4"><div class="flex items-start gap-3 sm:gap-2.5"><div class="bg-yellow text-purple-deep flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg sm:size-8"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="lucide lucide-book-open size-4 sm:size-3.5" fill="none" height="24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24" width="24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">